  "claim": "The Gannett company owns a daily newspaper that another newspaper comes in third place behind in the largest newspapers produced in Nevada. The Nevada School of Law was moved to its plant. Croatian Journalist Henry Rust Mighels was the editor of the other newspaper.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Nevada School of Law at Old College. Sentence: After its first year, the school moved from the former St. Thomas Aquinas Parochial School to its permanent home at the old \"Reno Gazette-Journal\" newspaper plant donated by the Gannett Company.\nPage: Reno Gazette-Journal. Sentence: The Reno Gazette-Journal is the main daily newspaper for Reno, Nevada.\nPage: Reno Gazette-Journal. Sentence: It is owned by the Gannett Company.\nPage: Nevada Appeal. Sentence: It is the state's third-largest paper, behind the \"Las Vegas Review-Journal\" and \"Reno Gazette-Journal\".\nPage: Henry Rust Mighels. Sentence: A writer of the Sagebrush School, he was the editor and publisher of Carson City, Nevada's \"Nevada Appeal\".",
