        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f0b72302-5f11-58e6-86d4-34cd1c9f0274",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Nevada School of Law at Old College, Gannett Company\n- Products: Reno Gazette-Journal, Nevada Appeal, Las Vegas Review-Journal\n- Places: Reno, Nevada, Carson City, Nevada\n- People: Henry Rust Mighels\n- Concepts: Sagebrush School\n\nFacts:\n- After its first year, the Nevada School of Law at Old College moved from the former St. Thomas Aquinas Parochial School to the old Reno Gazette-Journal newspaper plant as its permanent home.\n- Gannett Company donated the old Reno Gazette-Journal newspaper plant to the Nevada School of Law at Old College.\n- The Reno Gazette-Journal is the main daily newspaper for Reno, Nevada.\n- The Reno Gazette-Journal is owned by Gannett Company.\n- The Nevada Appeal is the third-largest newspaper in Nevada, behind the Las Vegas Review-Journal and the Reno Gazette-Journal.\n- Henry Rust Mighels was a writer of the Sagebrush School.\n- Henry Rust Mighels was the editor and publisher of the Nevada Appeal in Carson City, Nevada.",
